<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Sept 26.</title>
<headline>RTRS-AWB Australian wheat indicator prices - Sept 26.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1996-09-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>International prices for milling and Durum wheat were unchanged with no fresh market in puts in any direction, the Australian Wheat Board (AWB) said.</p>
<p>Wheat indicator prices for multi-grade contracts 96/97 and Durum were unchanged. Prices, FOB, in A$ per tonne:</p>
<p>		    ASW 10 pct		   No 1 DURUM</p>
<p>		    Delivered Port	     Delivered Port</p>
<p>Queensland</p>
<p>    Brisbane	156.75</p>
<p>    Gladstone     n/a</p>
<p>    Mackay	  n/a</p>
<p>New South Wales</p>
<p>    Newcastle     159.75			 199.00</p>
<p>    Port Kembla   160.75</p>
<p>Victoria</p>
<p>    Geelong	 161.00</p>
<p>    Portland	161.75</p>
<p>South Australia</p>
<p>    Port Adelaide 161.75			 198.00</p>
<p>    Port Giles    162.50</p>
<p>Port Lincoln  164.00</p>
<p>    Port Pirie    158.50</p>
<p>    Thevenard     159.00</p>
<p>    Wallaroo	160.25</p>
<p>Western Australia</p>
<p>    Albany	  167.25</p>
<p>    Esperance     165.75</p>
<p>    Fremantle     170.00</p>
<p>    Geraldton     167.00</p>
<p>NOTE: The indicator price represents the current state of the international wheat market. It is a cash contract price offered today by the AWB for wheat delivered during the 1996/97 harvest. The offer is valid until 4.30 p.m. Australian Eastern Standard Time (0630 GMT) and Eastern Standard Summer Time (0530 GMT). Indicator prices will be revised daily until October.</p>
<p>-- Sydney Newsroom 61-2 9373-1800</p>
